                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Beats Of Fury is a sort of rhythm game, well kind of... that has finally left Early Access after more than six years and it isn't exactly a great game or anything close to being a good one to begin with. The fact that I even spent 3.5 hours with it is honestly surprising, because it's not even a little bit of a joyride. It simply doesn't feel good to play and as for most of the music in the game I'd rather listen to my toilet flush for an hour. And since some reviewers have been spouting absolute nonsense like \"cool/good... amazing game\" someone needs to step in, shake their head in disbelief and simply say No da f--- it's not!\n\nAnd now to top it off they recently changed the capsule art to something that looks very much like partially or patchily assembled AI generated smut. Even more obvious was the slop infested new trailer where you could spot several AI artifacts if you paused at the right moments. After I pointed it out the devs quietly replaced the video and deleted my post about it on the forum. But hey it's already too late.\n\nBetween that, several other things I've noticed and the complete lack of any AI disclosure from the devs, I've not only lost what little interest I still had in the game, I've also lost trust in both the product and the people behind it. If I could I'd definitely get a refund. \n\nBetter stay away from this one. \n\nBy the way, greetings to Gilligames, Shaw&Nickeyson, Ussistant Studio, PartTimeIndie and some others. Soon you’ll see what’s coming your way.",
